00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:30.820
Now we're going to cover some more niche types
of peeks though, starting out with Re-peeking.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:34.750
As you probably guessed, this is when you
peek an angle, and then peek that same angle

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:38.789
again in the exact same way.
Generally speaking, don't do this.

00:07:38.789 --> 00:07:42.330
Repeeking is bad, because your enemies already
know your location, and they only have to

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:47.020
aim at one place, and it's the same place
where you just peeked. where as you don't

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:52.730
really quite know what to expect on the other
side.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:57.110
Repeeking can be good if you catch an enemy
in a bad position, but just as with any of

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:59.699
these other peeks, you'll have to use your
own discretion.

00:07:59.699 --> 00:08:03.750
As a rule of thumb though, i'm telling you,
peeking the same angle twice, is not a good

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.629
idea.
Try to mix up your peeks. Peek from one side,

00:08:06.629 --> 00:08:09.259
and then peek from another.
As we mentioned earlier, throw in a jiggle,

00:08:09.259 --> 00:08:43.100
then a wide swing, mix it up, keep your opponents

00:08:43.100 --> 00:09:42.420
on their toes.
That's all the peeks we're going to cover

